cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Evaluating LLM-Generated Hardware for Quantum Circuit Simulation
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata
  below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Krishna
    family-names: Patel
    affiliation: University of North Texas
  - given-names: Sumera
    family-names: Anjum
    affiliation: University of North Texas
  - given-names: Spencer
    family-names: Buchanan
    affiliation: University of Houston-Clear Lake
  - given-names: Xuechen
    family-names: Zhang
    affiliation: Kennesaw State University
  - given-names: Yunhe
    family-names: Feng
    affiliation: University of North Texas
  - given-names: Xiaokun
    family-names: Yang
    affiliation: University of Houston-Clear Lake
year: 2026
repository-code: https://github.com/IC-Design-Lab/LLM-Quantum-Emulator
abstract: >-
  Two studies on generating the top-level SystemVerilog of an FPGA
  quantum-circuit emulator with language models. The first characterises how
  prompt-only generation fails across models, prompt detail and input format,
  over 661 runs. The second supplies the family's gate map, exact port lists and
  composition rulebook as preloaded context plus one structurally matched worked
  example, reaching 53 of 55 circuits matching their golden state across 2-, 3-
  and 5-qubit families. Correctness is decided by simulation against a
  Qiskit-derived golden statevector rather than by comparison with a reference
  implementation.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - hardware description languages
  - SystemVerilog
  - quantum circuit simulation
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - FPGA acceleration
license: MIT
# The MIT license does not extend to the SystemVerilog that is output of the lab's
# Chisel generator or derived from it:
#   generation-study/gate_library/*.sv
#   generation-study/ground_truth/*.sv
#   generation-study/experiment/ground_truth/*.sv
#   generation-study/experiment/matched_arms/ground_truth/_lib_shared.sv
#   generation-study/experiment/matched_arms/ground_truth/_lib_sx.sv
#   generation-study/experiment/matched_arms/ground_truth/gate_library_flat_07_08.sv
#   rag-cag-system/corpus/code_examples/*/*_ground_truth.sv
#   rag-cag-system/results/vivado/synthesis-inputs/support/*_gen_support.sv
#   rag-cag-system/rag/output_v2/ShorFixed.sv
#   rag-cag-system/results/vivado/synthesis-inputs/designs/ShorFixed.sv
# Everything else is covered. See docs/hardware-provenance.md.

